## With a library input (peer.dll, of which spill.o uses nothing), phase 2's
## ldtoken of its export class follows the touch (without spilling, phase 2
## alone: shared-two-phase.test's TOK).
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj peer.ll -o peer.o
# RUN: msil-ld -shared peer.o -o peer.dll 2>&1 | count 0
# RUN: msil-ld -shared --msil-type-member-limit=4 spill.o peer.dll -o lib/spill.dll 2>&1 | count 0
# RUN: llvm-cil-dump lib/spill.dll > lib.txt
# RUN: %{listing} method lib.txt '<Module>' .cctor | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LIB-TOUCH
# LIB-TOUCH:      {{^}}  .method '.cctor' void() flags=0x1891 impl=0x0000{{$}}
# LIB-TOUCH-NEXT: {{^}}    .maxstack 1{{$}}
# LIB-TOUCH-NEXT: {{^}}    L0: ldsfld native int '<msil>Data'::'<msil>data'{{$}}
# LIB-TOUCH-NEXT: {{^}}    L1: pop{{$}}
# LIB-TOUCH-NEXT: {{^}}    L2: ldtoken [peer]peer{{$}}
# LIB-TOUCH-NEXT: {{^}}    L3: pop{{$}}
# LIB-TOUCH-NEXT: {{^}}    L4: ret{{$}}
# LIB-TOUCH-NOT:  {{.}}

## msil64-unknown-dotnet, listed with --forms=canon (short branches print
## long; the labels are instruction numbers): the guard's ten instructions
## L0-L9 as portable-guard.test pins them, then the touch, then (with
## peer.dll) the ldtoken; without the limit the guard alone; the guard's two
## failure blocks follow the last ret.
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj -mtriple=msil64-unknown-dotnet spill.ll -o dotnet/spill.o
# RUN: msil-ld -shared --msil-type-member-limit=4 dotnet/spill.o -o dotnet/spill.dll 2>&1 | count 0
# RUN: llvm-cil-dump --forms=canon dotnet/spill.dll > dotnet.txt
# RUN: %{listing} method dotnet.txt '<Module>' .cctor | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=GUARD,DOTNET-TOUCH
# RUN: msil-ld -shared dotnet/spill.o -o dotnet-nolimit/spill.dll 2>&1 | count 0
# RUN: llvm-cil-dump --forms=canon dotnet-nolimit/spill.dll > dotnet-nolimit.txt
# RUN: %{listing} method dotnet-nolimit.txt '<Module>' .cctor | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=GUARD,DOTNET-PLAIN
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj -mtriple=msil64-unknown-dotnet peer.ll -o dotnet/peer.o
# RUN: msil-ld -shared dotnet/peer.o -o dotnet/peer.dll 2>&1 | count 0
# RUN: msil-ld -shared --msil-type-member-limit=4 dotnet/spill.o dotnet/peer.dll -o dotnet-lib/spill.dll 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | count 0
# RUN: llvm-cil-dump --forms=canon dotnet-lib/spill.dll > dotnet-lib.txt
# RUN: %{listing} method dotnet-lib.txt '<Module>' .cctor | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=GUARD,DOTNET-LIB
# GUARD:             {{^}}  .method '.cctor' void() flags=0x1891 impl=0x0000{{$}}
# GUARD:             {{^}}    L0: ldc.i4.m1{{$}}
# GUARD-NEXT:        {{^}}    L1: conv.i{{$}}
# GUARD-NEXT:        {{^}}    L2: conv.u8{{$}}
# GUARD-NEXT:        {{^}}    L3: ldc.i8 -1{{$}}
# GUARD-NEXT:        {{^}}    L4: bne.un L[[#WIDTH:]]{{$}}
# GUARD-NEXT:        {{^}}    L5: ldc.i4.1{{$}}
# GUARD-NEXT:        {{^}}    L6: call uint8[](int32) [mscorlib]System.BitConverter::'GetBytes'{{$}}
# GUARD-NEXT:        {{^}}    L7: ldc.i4.0{{$}}
# GUARD-NEXT:        {{^}}    L8: ldelem.u1{{$}}
# GUARD-NEXT:        {{^}}    L9: brfalse L[[#ORDER:]]{{$}}
# DOTNET-TOUCH-NEXT: {{^}}    L10: ldsfld native int '<msil>Data'::'<msil>data'{{$}}
# DOTNET-TOUCH-NEXT: {{^}}    L11: pop{{$}}
# DOTNET-TOUCH-NEXT: {{^}}    L12: ret{{$}}
# DOTNET-PLAIN-NEXT: {{^}}    L10: ret{{$}}
# DOTNET-LIB-NEXT:   {{^}}    L10: ldsfld native int '<msil>Data'::'<msil>data'{{$}}
# DOTNET-LIB-NEXT:   {{^}}    L11: pop{{$}}
# DOTNET-LIB-NEXT:   {{^}}    L12: ldtoken [peer]peer{{$}}
# DOTNET-LIB-NEXT:   {{^}}    L13: pop{{$}}
# DOTNET-LIB-NEXT:   {{^}}    L14: ret{{$}}
# GUARD-DAG:         {{^}}    L[[#WIDTH]]: ldstr "spill is built for msil64-unknown-dotnet and needs a 64-bit .NET process; this process is 32-bit"{{$}}
# GUARD-DAG:         {{^}}    L[[#WIDTH+1]]: newobj instance void(string) {{(class )?}}[mscorlib]System.PlatformNotSupportedException::'.ctor'{{$}}
# GUARD-DAG:         {{^}}    L[[#WIDTH+2]]: throw{{$}}
# GUARD-DAG:         {{^}}    L[[#ORDER]]: ldstr "spill is built for msil64-unknown-dotnet and needs a little-endian .NET process"{{$}}
# GUARD-DAG:         {{^}}    L[[#ORDER+1]]: newobj instance void(string) {{(class )?}}[mscorlib]System.PlatformNotSupportedException::'.ctor'{{$}}
# GUARD-DAG:         {{^}}    L[[#ORDER+2]]: throw{{$}}
# GUARD-NOT:         {{.}}

## A library without an image whose phase 1 only stores '<msil>fn_' fields
## (f0-f2 and pick's): '<msil>Data' then needs no '<msil>data', so at 4 its
## four fields fit and there is no touch; at 3 they spill, and '<msil>data'
## is made in '<msil>Data' for the touch alone, within the limit (setting
## the flag adds at most '<msil>data', so the decision to spill stays right;
## two of the four fields spill).
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj fnaddr.ll -o fnaddr.o
# RUN: msil-ld -shared --msil-type-member-limit=4 fnaddr.o -o fn4/fnaddr.dll 2>&1 | count 0
# RUN: llvm-cil-dump fn4/fnaddr.dll > fn4.txt
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/members.py --limit 4 fn4.txt | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FN4 \
# RUN:   --implicit-check-not='<msil>Spill' --implicit-check-not='<msil>data'
# FN4: {{^}}count <msil>Data methods=1 fields=4{{$}}
# FN4: {{^}}limit 4 ok{{$}}
# RUN: %{listing} method fn4.txt '<Module>' .cctor | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=NO-TOUCH
# RUN: msil-ld -shared --msil-type-member-limit=3 fnaddr.o -o fn3/fnaddr.dll 2>&1 | count 0
# RUN: llvm-cil-dump fn3/fnaddr.dll > fn3.txt
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/members.py --limit 3 fn3.txt | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FN3
# FN3: {{^}}field <msil>Data::<msil>data flags=0x0033{{$}}
# FN3: {{^}}count <msil>Data methods=1 fields=3{{$}}
# FN3: {{^}}count <msil>Spill1 methods={{[0-9]+}} fields=2{{$}}
# FN3: {{^}}limit 3 ok{{$}}
# RUN: %{listing} method fn3.txt '<Module>' .cctor | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=TOUCH

## Fields that spill with no phase 1: weak.ll's three weak symbols stay
## undefined, so their address fields are never stored and '<msil>Data' has
## no '.cctor' (nothing to race with); a touch needs a phase 1
## (buildTrailer's precondition), so <Module>::.cctor, which calls the
## constructor, has none, and the link stays silent.
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj weak.ll -o weak.o
# RUN: msil-ld -shared --msil-type-member-limit=2 weak.o -o weak/weak.dll 2>&1 | count 0
# RUN: llvm-cil-dump weak/weak.dll > weak.txt
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/members.py --limit 2 weak.txt | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=WEAK
# WEAK: {{^}}count <msil>Data methods=0 fields=2{{$}}
# WEAK: {{^}}count <msil>Spill1 methods=1 fields=1{{$}}
# WEAK: {{^}}limit 2 ok{{$}}
# RUN: %{listing} method weak.txt '<Module>' .cctor | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=WEAK-CCTOR
# WEAK-CCTOR:      {{^}}  .method '.cctor' void() flags=0x1891 impl=0x0000{{$}}
# WEAK-CCTOR-NEXT: {{^}}    .maxstack 0{{$}}
# WEAK-CCTOR-NEXT: {{^}}    L0: call void() '{{[^']+}}'::'probe'{{$}}
# WEAK-CCTOR-NEXT: {{^}}    L1: ret{{$}}
# WEAK-CCTOR-NOT:  {{.}}

## Spill classes that hold only methods: at 3, methods.ll's six internal
## functions fill <Module> and spill into '<msil>Spill1' and
## '<msil>Spill2', while the three fields of '<msil>Data' ('<msil>data', g
## and '<msil>fn_use') fit. The library has a phase 1 but no touch, and no
## <Module>::.cctor: the touch is keyed on the fields of '<msil>Data'
## spilling, so a rule keyed on any spill class, or on methods or fields
## over the limit, would add one here.
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj methods.ll -o methods.o
# RUN: msil-ld -shared --msil-type-member-limit=3 methods.o -o methods.dll 2>&1 | count 0
# RUN: llvm-cil-dump methods.dll > methods.txt
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/members.py --limit 3 methods.txt \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=METHODS --implicit-check-not='field <msil>Spill'
# METHODS: {{^}}count <msil>Data methods=1 fields=3{{$}}
# METHODS: {{^}}count <msil>Spill1 methods=2 fields=0{{$}}
# METHODS: {{^}}count <msil>Spill2 methods=1 fields=0{{$}}
# METHODS: {{^}}limit 3 ok{{$}}
# RUN: %{listing} method methods.txt '<Module>' .cctor | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=NO-TOUCH

## Data imports: environ on linux-gnu, against the libc.so.6 stub.
# RUN: yaml2obj --docnum=1 %S/Inputs/native/glibc.yaml -o libc.o
# RUN: ld.lld -shared -soname libc.so.6 --version-script %S/Inputs/native/glibc-libc.map libc.o -o libc.so.6
